# s1-page-virtual: the desktop operation that reaches the new core method `projectFs/localPage/virtual`.

file: apps/desktop/src/shared/core-lanes/desktop-operation-route.ts
place: the "local pages served by the core page server" block, after `localPageUrlIn`
add: localPageVirtualIn: positional('projectFs/localPage/virtual', ['files', 'ownerId']),
     files is the array [{ path, dataBase64 | text, type }]; the caller (visualize host-pane-preview / host-export-path, via CoreLocalPages)
     maps each VirtualPageFile { type, body: Buffer } of a Record<string, ...> to { path: <key>, dataBase64: body.toString('base64'), type }.
place: CUSTOM_REPLY (next to `projectEntryPathIn`)
add: localPageVirtualIn: (reply) => record(reply).url,
     the core answers {url}; Node's localVirtualPageUrl returned the URL string, so the route unwraps it (not SAME_REPLY: that passes the
     core's JSON through unchanged, which is right for localPageUrlIn only because projectFs/localPageUrl answers a bare string).

file: apps/desktop/src/main/core-local-pages.ts (task that moves the visualize callers to the core)
place: interface CoreLocalPages
add: virtualUrl(files: Record<string, { type: string; body: Buffer }>, access?: { ownerId?: string; owner?: PageOwner }): Promise<string>
     through invoke<string>('localPageVirtualIn', [...]) with the same owner watch (revokeOwner on 'destroyed') as url().
